<openings>
The story hasn't begun, so <this_scene> above has no place or time yet. Offer the owner three ways to open its first scene, for them to pick from. Each is a line or two for the owner to read: where and when the scene opens, and what is happening as {{ protagonist }} comes into it. Make them true to the setup and different in kind: say, a quiet start, a start in the middle of trouble, and one the owner wouldn't expect.

Call offer_openings with the three, and write nothing else.
